From 69695ec30df559c4a8c2abcac4670b98474a66bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 00:14:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix etymology feature: subject id mismatch broke it site-wide

LEAEtymology.decorate() and the etymology hint in run.html checked the
subject id against 'history-of-architecture', but the actual id in
data/subjects.json is 'history' (the data folder is named
history-of-architecture, the id isn't). That mismatch meant the check
never passed, so no term was ever decorated on any History module.

Also bump the shared-asset cache-busting version to ?v=16 (was still
?v=1 on etymology.js while everything else sat at ?v=15) so this isn't
stuck behind GitHub Pages' 10-minute asset cache after deploy.
